INT-361 makes the NovaShell splitter honour a backslash and keep case ... esac whole. Today split_semicolons_marked (zero/shell/novashell/src/main.rs:340; plain loop 384-404, ; arm 395), line_has_compound (459), split_around_compounds (510) and split_logical (expand.rs:565) track quotes but not the backslash, and the word list in word_at (main.rs:423) and the opener matches (490, 569) know for, while, until and if but not case. Measured on a box build of origin/main 50f22621 (novashell 6.1.3), nsh -c against bash -c: find -exec ... \; fails with missing argument to -exec; find \( ... \) is cut into three pieces; echo a\;b prints a\ and tries to run b; echo "a\"b; echo c" runs echo c as a second command; case x in a) echo A;; x) echo X;; esac is cut at ;; and fails. After this, a backslash outside single quotes keeps the next character in the piece in those four scanners, and case opens a region that esac closes, the same shape as if and fi, so try_shell_construct (engine.rs:1757) sends it to sh whole. A box prototype passed cargo +1.88.0 test -p novashell 313 of 313 (308 before plus five int361_ tests) and made all 13 measured probe lines match bash. Gates: red int361_ splitter tests first, then the fix, then a box nsh -c versus bash -c proof, then four nsh-test conformance cases, then the laptop. Out of scope: brace groups, a ( ) group followed by a redirect, pipe or &, time ( ), ${VAR:-default} and other ${...} forms in the spine, legacy NSH_SPINE=0 output, and merging the splitters (foundation item 8). Bump is novashell patch and nsh-test patch. Agents push branch int-361 only; Eric reviews; Christian merges, seals, ships and runs nsh-test, doors and d on the laptop.
